{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791567579,"nonce":"bV0oecjmQLKuG5L7lsnsKzTe1yk=","message":"Step 3 done locally, not pushed: 621fe8bcb1ccedf4fdccd46abfe3b3177863c115 (Div::show_when) and 07854294e53f05599f91803a42b61e25bc1e00ac (reactive Text font properties), on top of the fix in f72b41453ebef366b5415f86b50c66167ba241f5 (a7f6d8a).\n\n- Display: Div::show_when takes a bool, a signal or a computed and flips display: none in place. The display it returns to is read at build time, so it is the one the element was built with whatever the builder call order. Not a new write kind: a layout write.\n- Text size, color, weight, letter_spacing and line_height take a signal or computed. A change writes the matching RenderProps override (paint already honours them) and the layout sync carries it into the box. No new write kind either. A text with any binding is measured through a context.\n- Found on the way, fixed in 793cfcb096ebc87aebe746d6457989440185e756 (01dd94a): display: none did not hide text; a hidden subtree's text drew one letter per line at the corner. A bound Display would not have worked without it.\n- Not done: italic, and font family. FontFamily and Overflow still have no writers.\n\nNext is step 4: move cn's display-only closures onto these (the slider value text, reactive_node's labels, the button label).","files":null}]}